  <story>
    <asA>developer</asA>
    <iWant>architectural decisions automatically inferred from configuration files and package manifests</iWant>
    <soThat>the knowledge graph captures the "why" behind technology choices even for existing projects</soThat>
    <tasks>
      <task id="1" ac="1">Implement config file reader
        <subtask>Create /home/ubuntu/scripts/bootstrap-decisions.mjs — decision inference orchestrator</subtask>
        <subtask>Discover and read config/manifest files: package.json, tsconfig.json, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, .env.example, README.md, .eslintrc.*, .prettierrc.*, jest.config.*, vite.config.*, next.config.*, tailwind.config.*, webpack.config.*</subtask>
        <subtask>Parse package.json dependencies and devDependencies — classify into categories (framework, state management, routing, styling, testing, build tools, utilities)</subtask>
        <subtask>Parse tsconfig.json for compiler options that reflect architectural choices (strict mode, path aliases, target, module resolution)</subtask>
        <subtask>Parse Docker/compose files for deployment and infrastructure decisions</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="2" ac="2,3,6">Implement decision inference agent step
        <subtask>Create agent prompt for the Decision Inferrer role — analyzes config data and produces decision articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Infer framework decision (e.g., React, Next.js, Vue, Express) from dependencies and config files</subtask>
        <subtask>Infer database decision from dependencies (e.g., prisma, mongoose, pg, dynamodb-toolbox) and connection configs</subtask>
        <subtask>Infer auth approach from dependencies and code patterns (e.g., jwt, passport, next-auth, cognito)</subtask>
        <subtask>Infer styling decision from dependencies and configs (e.g., Tailwind, styled-components, CSS modules, SCSS)</subtask>
        <subtask>Infer build/bundler decision from configs and scripts (e.g., Vite, webpack, esbuild, Next.js built-in)</subtask>
        <subtask>Infer testing strategy from dependencies and configs (e.g., Jest, Vitest, Playwright, Cypress)</subtask>
        <subtask>Infer deployment strategy from Docker, CI/CD configs, and package.json scripts</subtask>
        <subtask>Set maturity between 0.3 (weak inference) and 0.5 (strong evidence) based on number of config signals</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="3" ac="2,3,4">Generate decision articles
        <subtask>Write decision articles to knowledge/decisions/ using naming convention {category}-{choice}.md (e.g., framework-nextjs.md, styling-tailwind.md)</subtask>
        <subtask>Each article follows standard wiki format with frontmatter: type: decision, phase: solutioning, status: active</subtask>
        <subtask>Include ## Context section with inferred rationale from usage patterns</subtask>
        <subtask>Include ## Chosen Option with the detected technology and version</subtask>
        <subtask>Include ## Evidence listing specific files and config entries that demonstrate the choice</subtask>
        <subtask>Include empty ## Alternatives Considered section for future user refinement</subtask>
        <subtask>Add INFORMS edges via [[wikilinks]] in an ## Informs section pointing to code articles that use the decision</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="4" ac="5,7">Generate architecture overview
        <subtask>Create knowledge/solutioning/architecture-overview.md — a synthesized summary of all inferred decisions, tech stack diagram, and project structure overview</subtask>
        <subtask>Include [[wikilinks]] to each decision article and key code articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Set frontmatter: type: architecture, phase: solutioning, status: active, maturity: 0.4</subtask>
        <subtask>Update knowledge/index.md with all new decision articles and the architecture overview</subtask>
        <subtask>Append decision inference record to knowledge/log.md</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="5" ac="1">Pipeline integration
        <subtask>Register as stage 3 of the brownfield-bootstrap pipeline (runs after scan, can run in parallel with deps stage)</subtask>
        <subtask>Emit pipeline events: { type: progress, stage: decisions, decisionsInferred: X }</subtask>
        <subtask>Log summary: decisions inferred, config files analyzed, maturity distribution</subtask>
      </task>
    </tasks>
  </story>

  <acceptanceCriteria>
    <criterion id="1">The decision inference agent reads package.json, tsconfig.json, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, .env.example, README.md, and other config/manifest files in the project root</criterion>
    <criterion id="2">Decision articles are created in knowledge/decisions/ for major technology choices: framework, database, auth provider, styling approach, bundler, testing framework, deployment strategy, etc.</criterion>
    <criterion id="3">Each decision article includes: Context (inferred from usage patterns), Chosen Option (the technology/approach detected), Evidence (which files and configs demonstrate the choice), and Alternatives Considered (left empty for user refinement)</criterion>
    <criterion id="4">Decision articles have INFORMS edges (via [[wikilinks]]) to the code articles that use/implement them</criterion>
    <criterion id="5">A synthesized architecture overview article is created at knowledge/solutioning/architecture-overview.md summarizing all inferred decisions</criterion>
    <criterion id="6">Decision articles are assigned lower maturity (0.3-0.5) since they are reverse-engineered, not explicitly documented</criterion>
    <criterion id="7">knowledge/index.md is updated to include all new decision and solutioning articles</criterion>
  </acceptanceCriteria>

