  <constraints>
    <constraint type="maturity">Inferred decisions use lower maturity: 0.3 for weak inference (single config signal), 0.5 for strong evidence (multiple config files and widespread usage). This signals to users and agents that these decisions should be reviewed and refined.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Decision articles use INFORMS edges (not DEPENDS_ON) to link to code articles. INFORMS has weight 0.3 reflecting advisory rather than structural relationships. The ## Informs section maps to outgoing INFORMS edges per architecture doc section 3.2.</constraint>
    <constraint type="parallelism">This story can run in parallel with Story 6.2 since both read from Story 6.1 output but write to different wiki directories (decisions/ and solutioning/ vs. code/).</constraint>
    <constraint type="completeness">Alternatives Considered section is intentionally left empty. These are reverse-engineered decisions — the original alternatives were not documented. Users refine later.</constraint>
    <constraint type="accuracy">Decision inference must be evidence-based. Every detected technology choice must cite specific files and config entries in the Evidence section. Speculative inferences without file evidence should not be created.</constraint>
  </constraints>

